  "notes": "USAGE:\n{親|した}しむ means to feel close to or enjoy something over time. The passive form {親|した}しまれる (to be loved/enjoyed by many) is extremely common. Do not confuse with {親|した}しい (adjective: close, intimate, friendly), though they share the same root.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {自然|しぜん}に{親|した}しむ: to enjoy/appreciate nature\n- {文化|ぶんか}に{親|した}しむ: to become familiar with culture\n- {親|した}しまれる: to be loved/enjoyed (by many)\n- {広|ひろ}く{親|した}しまれている: widely beloved\n- {読書|どくしょ}に{親|した}しむ: to enjoy reading",
